    description: "Per WI-duroz human approval: implement a lightweight variant of WI-botol (the full 200-repo prospecting run). Select 20-30 polyglot repos from the pool, run dead-code-maybe --exclude-annotated on each, group candidates by gap kind (yaml_unmarshal, cobra_cli, memberlist, pipeline_stage, etc.), and rank by frequency across the corpus.\n\nDeliverable: a single JSON/CSV artifact under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/prospector_runs/<timestamp>/ with top-ranked candidates and per-category counts. Unlike WI-botol, this is explicitly NOT wired into a recurring bakeoff cycle — it is a one-shot tool for prioritizing linker investment.\n\nHigher priority than WI-botol because the lightweight variant is faster to implement and provides actionable signal sooner. Blocks WI-botol: the full 200-repo run should only proceed if the lightweight variant demonstrates clear value.\n\nDependencies: base dead-code-maybe (done), --exclude-annotated filter (done, PR #2907), cross-language string collision (done, PR #2904)."  # b12a
